entries.html:
This object lets a Mini App hosted on <a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots/serverless">Telegram Serverless</a> call the bot's <a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots/serverless#endpoints">endpoints</a> – the server-side functions of the Mini App. Each call is sent together with the Mini App's <i>initData</i>, which the platform validates before running the endpoint, so the endpoint always knows which user is calling it.

• call(name[, input][, callback]) (<i>Function</i>) — A method that calls the endpoint with the specified name. The optional <i>input</i> parameter is a JSON-serializable object that is passed to the endpoint as its first argument. If an optional <i>callback</i> parameter was passed, the <i>callback</i> function will be called. In case of an error, the first argument will contain the error. In case of success, the first argument will be <i>null</i> and the value returned by the endpoint will be passed as the second argument.

The error passed to the <i>callback</i> function is an <i>Error</i> object with the following additional fields:

• message (<i>String</i>) — A human-readable description of the error.
• type (<i>String</i>) — <i>Optional</i>. The type of the error returned by the platform. “ENDPOINT_ERROR” if the endpoint refused the call by throwing an <i>EndpointError</i>. Other values indicate errors reported by the platform, such as “UNAUTHORIZED” if <i>initData</i> is missing or invalid.
• status (<i>Integer</i>) — The HTTP status code of the response, or <i>0</i> if the request could not be completed.
• parameters (<i>Object</i>) — <i>Optional</i>. Additional data passed by the endpoint along with its <i>EndpointError</i>.

<pre><code>Telegram.WebApp.Serverless.call('getProfile', {lang: 'en'}, function(error, profile) {
  if (error) {
    console.error(error.message);
    return;
  }
  console.log(profile);
});</code></pre>

